# subagents-bench credentials and settings.
#
# scripts/setup.sh copies this file to .env (gitignored, chmod 600) if .env is
# missing. Fill in the values, then re-run scripts/setup.sh to verify them.
# .env never overrides a variable that is already set in your shell.
# Never commit .env.

# --- Required ------------------------------------------------------------
# Sail Research API key: the DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash orchestrator and the Gemma
# subagents in configs/sweeps/{smoke,pilot}.yaml. https://sailresearch.com
SAIL_API_KEY=

# --- Prime Intellect (only for configs/sweeps/prime_size.yaml) -------------
# Either uncomment and set both here, or run `prime login` once: the prime
# CLI stores api_key and team_id in ~/.prime/config.json and the harness reads
# them from there. The team id is sent as X-Prime-Team-ID; without it requests
# bill the personal account instead of the team. (Optional variables stay
# commented out so an empty value never shadows the prime CLI config.)
# PRIME_API_KEY=
# PRIME_TEAM_ID=

# --- Optional ------------------------------------------------------------
# Only for configs that use these providers (configs/unified.yaml and the
# baselines use an Anthropic orchestrator; provider: openai/vllm endpoints).
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Cloud sandboxes instead of local Docker (harbor.env in the sweep spec):
# set the variables your harbor environment needs, e.g.
# DAYTONA_API_KEY=
# MODAL_TOKEN_ID=
# MODAL_TOKEN_SECRET=

# Where `harbor dataset download` exports task definitions
# (default: <repo>/.cache/datasets).
# SUBAGENTS_BENCH_DATASET_CACHE=
